      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city became a township in 1814, a village in 1914, and a city on November 12, 1960.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.independenceohio.org/about/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Independence Historical Society, founded in 1966, preserves the city’s unique history and hosts events at Historic Hall and the Bramley House.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.independencehistoricalsociety.com/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A mural painted in 2018 by Oscar Velasquez at 6576 Brecksville Road tells the story of Independence’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.independencehistoricalsociety.com/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Cuyahoga Valley Scenic Railroad offers heritage rides through the region, connecting Independence to the national park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.independenceohio.org/about/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Independence sits at the intersection of I‑480 and I‑77, a major interchange that opened in 1940 and expanded in the 1950s.",
